.\" File: man/femtoctl.8
.\" Created by Andrea "Nemesi" Cocito on 08/11/2026
.\" FemtoFS resident-bank administration manual.
.Dd November 8, 2026
.Dt FEMTOCTL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm femtoctl
.Nd administer resident FemtoFS image banks
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm list
.Nm
.Cm add
.Ar label path
.Nm
.Cm discard
.Ar label
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility administers banks through
.Pa /dev/femtofs .
The kernel module must be loaded and the caller must have root privileges.
Labels contain 1 to 63 ASCII letters, digits, underscores or hyphens.
.Bl -tag -width "discard label"
.It Cm list
Print a tab-separated table with columns
.Dv LABEL , ORIGIN , BYTES , ALLOCATED , STATE , UUID , SUPPLIED_SOURCE .
Origin is
.Cm loader
for adopted preload memory or
.Cm copy
for imported images.
Sizes distinguish logical image bytes from allocated backing bytes.
State is
.Cm claimed
or
.Cm available .
The source column is the supplied name or path string, not a persistent
reference to the source object.
.It Cm add Ar label path
Synchronously copy the complete image from a regular file or readable,
seekable character device into wired RAM, validate it, and publish the bank.
The label must be unused.
GEOM disk sources are supported when their read alignment is compatible.
Keep the source unchanged throughout import for a coherent snapshot.
The source is released after import; later changes or device removal cannot
affect the bank.
An allocation failure reports an out-of-memory error.
Asynchronous import is not implemented.
.It Cm discard Ar label
Release an unmounted bank and its metadata.
Discarding a claimed bank fails as busy.
A discarded loader bank cannot be mounted again unless populated anew.
Discard every bank before unloading the kernel module.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /dev/femtofs
.It Pa /dev/femtofs
Administrator-only ioctl endpoint.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
femtoctl add data /path/to/data.0fs
femtoctl list
mount_femtofs -o clean data /mnt
umount /mnt
femtoctl discard data
kldunload femtofs
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr femtofs 5 ,
.Xr kldload 8 ,
.Xr kldunload 8 ,
.Xr makefemtofs 8 ,
.Xr mount_femtofs 8
